## Original Content
Five political parties have won seats in Kazakhstan's first election to the country's new unicameral parliament, the Kurultai, according to preliminary results released on Monday by the Central Election Commission.

## Summary
Kazakhstan held its first election to a new unicameral parliament called the Kurultai, where five political parties have won seats according to preliminary results. The Central Election Commission released these results on Monday.

## Key Points
- This is Kazakhstan's first election to a unicameral parliament.
- The parliament is named Kurultai.
- Five political parties secured seats in the election.
- Preliminary results were announced by the Central Election Commission.


